From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Goyvaerts <jonathan.goyvaerts@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 19:06:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] usb: typec: tipd: clear a failed partner, report a failed
 role change

tps6598x_connect() left an ERR_PTR in tps->partner when
typec_register_partner() failed. Its "already connected" check then
treated the port as connected, so no later connect could register the
partner. Clear it, as the cd321x path does.

tps6598x_dr_set() ignored the result of tps6598x_set_data_role(), so a
role switch that failed was reported to the Type-C class as done.

Signed-off-by: Jonathan Goyvaerts <jonathan.goyvaerts@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: LLM
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
---
 drivers/usb/typec/tipd/core.c | 9 ++++++---
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/typec/tipd/core.c b/drivers/usb/typec/tipd/core.c
index cd7b544cc6..979d99b923 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/typec/tipd/core.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/tipd/core.c
@@ -272,8 +272,11 @@ static int tps6598x_connect(struct tps6598x *tps, u32 status)
 		return ret;
 
 	tps->partner = typec_register_partner(tps->port, &desc);
-	if (IS_ERR(tps->partner))
-		return PTR_ERR(tps->partner);
+	if (IS_ERR(tps->partner)) {
+		ret = PTR_ERR(tps->partner);
+		tps->partner = NULL;
+		return ret;
+	}
 
 	if (desc.identity)
 		typec_partner_set_identity(tps->partner);
@@ -437,7 +440,7 @@ static int tps6598x_dr_set(struct typec_port *port, enum typec_data_role role)
 		goto out_unlock;
 	}
 
-	tps6598x_set_data_role(tps, role, true);
+	ret = tps6598x_set_data_role(tps, role, true);
 
 out_unlock:
 	mutex_unlock(&tps->lock);
